    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Xylem transports water and dissolved minerals unidirectionally from roots to leaves, whereas Phloem conducts synthesized food bidirectionally.",
        "Ethylene is the only plant hormone that exists in a gaseous form and plays a crucial role in fruit ripening.",
        "Light-dependent reactions of photosynthesis take place in the thylakoid membranes (grana), while light-independent reactions occur in the stroma of chloroplasts."
      ],
      "id": "pjjxy9w"
